                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2bef5725-222d-3552-8d2c-238dde0feac2",
                        "entry_id": "9885214e-4f4d-3de0-8145-1214af63cea2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "w sposób wyrażający drwinę"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e828cc7-6934-487a-b253-313bbea7d6b3",
                                "sense_id": "2bef5725-222d-3552-8d2c-238dde0feac2",
                                "text": "Spróbujmy, może tym razem się uda! - wykrzyknął drwiąco."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10d1b7eb-62ec-4f2c-b6ae-8a0ab03764ea",
                        "source_entry_id": "9885214e-4f4d-3de0-8145-1214af63cea2",
                        "source_sense_id": "2bef5725-222d-3552-8d2c-238dde0feac2",
                        "target_lang_word": "mockingly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mockingly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8633f58-7a0f-3d3b-acb3-f50f104889ab",
                                        "entry_id": "d14d3fbf-4a22-39ee-b693-be5d0eb9ee5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Said, written, or done with the intent to mock, or ridicule; with mocking effect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ee631a8-5319-4006-b8e3-221fa32c7693",
                                                "sense_id": "f8633f58-7a0f-3d3b-acb3-f50f104889ab",
                                                "text": "I remember how mockingly bright the day seemed as I went back on my melancholy pilgrimage to the little house at Woking, how busy the streets and vivid the moving life about me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44fd91a3-2ce7-4e5c-be37-29652eaa80e2",
                                                "sense_id": "f8633f58-7a0f-3d3b-acb3-f50f104889ab",
                                                "text": "It then mockingly says they connect “like-minded Tesla owners with one another, facilitating a vibrant community through shared contact information.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d9094645-8793-4b72-a6c1-de57c4cb7e00",
                        "source_entry_id": "9885214e-4f4d-3de0-8145-1214af63cea2",
                        "source_sense_id": "2bef5725-222d-3552-8d2c-238dde0feac2",
                        "target_lang_word": "derisively",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "derisively",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84ea18ef-bd08-3fa7-8170-42fe586e01f3",
                                        "entry_id": "c14470eb-f613-3ceb-9e7b-eae545f46dbe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a derisive manner; demeaningly, mockingly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db47f658-1ee6-4864-8ee1-631267abfbcf",
                                                "sense_id": "84ea18ef-bd08-3fa7-8170-42fe586e01f3",
                                                "text": "As ſometimes, with us, a queſtion is put deriſively, in the form of an aſſertion, when the propoſer conceives, as ſeems to have happened here, ſome abſurdity in the thing, I thought it beſt, after the example of ſo many Lat[in] interpreters, to adopt the equivocal, or rather the oblique, form of the original expreſſion. The ambiguity is not real, but apparent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23d1c39b-eb3a-42f7-9530-77970fcfff76",
                                                "sense_id": "84ea18ef-bd08-3fa7-8170-42fe586e01f3",
                                                "text": "In the personal bearing of Gustavus Adolphus [of Sweden], more distinctly than in his high aims, it now became evident that he deemed himself free from the obligations of deference to others, and regarded his own aspirations as his sole standard of action; he expressed himself to the Marquis as disapproving of the French King's course because he did not set himself up as the reformer of his Church, and he spoke derisively of the Pope."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fe78e4b-f1fb-4f43-a9fd-71abc55de57e",
                                                "sense_id": "84ea18ef-bd08-3fa7-8170-42fe586e01f3",
                                                "text": "[\"]And suddenly he notices the workman at a distance standing there and smiling deceitfully, that is, not deceitfully though, I'm wrong there, what is it …?\" / \"Derisively,\" Versilov prompted him discreetly. / \"Derisively, yes, a little derisively, that kind, good Russian smile, you know; the great personage was in a bad humour, you understand: 'What are you waiting here for, big beard?' said he. 'Who are you?'\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7f4deaf-ed27-425e-a72a-1d5980988371",
                        "source_entry_id": "9885214e-4f4d-3de0-8145-1214af63cea2",
                        "source_sense_id": "2bef5725-222d-3552-8d2c-238dde0feac2",
                        "target_lang_word": "jeeringly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jeeringly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a41ed3dd-87a3-3e02-8bdd-34d4e5965054",
                                        "entry_id": "f2465b70-c2fd-36d6-8846-31a20cdf3ca7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a jeering manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b25fba4-185c-4195-8db8-af6fd4f063dd",
                                                "sense_id": "a41ed3dd-87a3-3e02-8bdd-34d4e5965054",
                                                "text": "You shall find by common experience how your superstitious false worshipers slight the Word of God; they are above it, they speak jeeringly of the Scripture and of warrants from Gods Word; Oh you must do nothing but you must have Scripture for it: They cry up Fathers and antiquity, and such and such Writers, but for the Word of God they usually contemn and scorn it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36b092f6-1c5d-4826-a051-5ae296d0d8b9",
                                                "sense_id": "a41ed3dd-87a3-3e02-8bdd-34d4e5965054",
                                                "text": "[…] they turned their Anger into ridiculing the Man, and his Sorrow for his Wife and Children; taunted him with want of Courage to leap into the great Pit, and go to Heaven, as they jeeringly express’d it, along with them, adding some very profane, and even blasphemous Expressions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99fc5743-4d5b-4333-b9e0-52922a65723a",
                                                "sense_id": "a41ed3dd-87a3-3e02-8bdd-34d4e5965054",
                                                "text": "The sea had jeeringly kept his finite body up, but drowned the infinite of his soul."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e4e6674-5d2d-461a-a593-a919d3acbd40",
                                                "sense_id": "a41ed3dd-87a3-3e02-8bdd-34d4e5965054",
                                                "text": "The Florentine winter lasts only from mid-December to March, and in that season there are luminous days, but there are also jeeringly cold nights and days together when the tramontana wind comes devastatingly down from the Alps three pinched days at a spell, blowing pitilessly […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
